<title>FRANCE: Alcatel keeps climbing on Thomson bid loss.</title>
<headline>Alcatel keeps climbing on Thomson bid loss.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Alcatel Alsthom Cie Generale d'Electricite' kept climbing in mid-afternoon on news the company had lost out in the bidding for Thomson SA.</p>
<p>Upgrades from brokerages Cheuvreux de Virieu, CCF Elysees Bourse and American bank Morgan Stanley gave the stock an extra boost in the afternoon.</p>
<p>At 1325 GMT Alcatel was trading at 458.7 francs, up 3.17 percent but off its high of 464.8 francs.</p>
<p>The share also benefitted from short-covering by investors who had sold in the belief that Alcatel would win the bidding for Thomson.</p>
<p>The shares of Lagardere Group, which won the bidding for Thomson, remained suspended, as did Thomson shares.</p>
</text>
